      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "# Cloud-Sea Glide: Flight and Generation Spec\n\n**Units:** metres, seconds, radians. Cloud top is y = 0. Integrate with a fixed step dt = 1/60.\n\n### Flight model\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Take-off | y = 80, v = 20, pitch θ = 0 |\n| Launch grace | θ locked at 0 for 3 s |\n| Hold (climb) | θ → +0.35 at 0.8 rad/s |\n| Release (dive) | θ → −0.35 at 0.25 rad/s |\n| Speed change | dv = (−5.9·sinθ − 0.0012·v²)·dt |\n| Speed limits | 12–42 |\n| Vertical speed | vy = v·sinθ − 1.0 − 0.5·\\|sin bank\\| |\n| Stall (v < 13) | θ forced down 0.5 rad/s |\n| Ceiling | y ≤ 140 |\n| Bank | ±0.6, roll rate 2.5 rad/s, returns to 0 when not steering |\n| Turn rate | yaw += 0.9·sin(bank)·dt (max 0.51 rad/s) |\n\n**No-input check (hand estimate):**\n- 0–3 s: about 3 m lost.\n- 3–4.4 s: about 5 m lost.\n- After that: about 9–11 m/s sink.\n- Clouds reached at about 11 s, which meets both the 6 s and 10 s targets.\n\n### Spawning\n- Spawn objects 600 m ahead along the heading. Despawn them 100 m behind.\n- Difficulty factor: d = min(1, distance/5000).\n\n| Object | Spacing | Lateral offset | Size / height |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Island | 90–150 × (1 − 0.4d) | ±120 | r 15–35 × (1 + 0.3d); top 20–90 |\n| Updraft | 220–320 × (1 + 0.5d) | ±50 | r 10; column 0–150 |\n| Orb | 40–70 | ±30 | y 25–90; pickup r 4 |\n\n**Safe start:**\n- The first island appears no closer than 450 m.\n- Within the first 600 m, islands keep a lateral offset of at least 40 m.\n\n**Difficulty growth:** base speed floor rises by 4d.\n\n### Collision\n- Islands are vertical cylinders spanning from (top − 40) to (top + 3).\n- A hit occurs when the horizontal distance is less than r + 1.5 and y is inside that span.\n- Updraft effect: vy += 14 while inside the column.\n- Cloud contact: y ≤ 0.5.\n\n### Scoring and restart\n- Score = floor(distance/10) + 10 per orb.\n- Best result is kept in a session variable only (resets when the page reloads).\n- Game over triggers on an island hit or cloud contact. The game freezes and shows distance, score and best.\n- After 0.6 s, Space, click, tap or R restarts the run. All state resets to take-off.\n\n**Unverified:**\n- These numbers have not been run in a simulation or playtested.\n- The timing figures are hand calculations only."
