      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "# Cloud-Sea Glide: Synthesized Sound Module\n\nThis code uses only Web Audio synthesis and loads no audio files. It has 30 lines and only declares functions and variables, so nothing runs when it is pasted. The `AudioContext` is created the first time `startWind()` is called, which must happen inside a user action such as keydown, pointerdown or touchstart.\n\n```js\nlet AC=null,master,noiseBuf,windF,windG;\nfunction noiseSrc(){const s=AC.createBufferSource();s.buffer=noiseBuf;s.loop=true;return s;}\nfunction env(peak,a,d){const g=AC.createGain(),t=AC.currentTime;g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001,t);g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(peak,t+a);g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001,t+a+d);g.connect(master);return g;}\nfunction startWind(){\n  if(AC){if(AC.state==='suspended')AC.resume();return;}\n  AC=new (window.AudioContext||window.webkitAudioContext)();\n  master=AC.createGain();master.gain.value=0.7;master.connect(AC.destination);\n  noiseBuf=AC.createBuffer(1,AC.sampleRate*2,AC.sampleRate);\n  const d=noiseBuf.getChannelData(0);for(let i=0;i<d.length;i++)d[i]=Math.random()*2-1;\n  windF=AC.createBiquadFilter();windF.type='bandpass';windF.frequency.value=400;windF.Q.value=0.7;\n  windG=AC.createGain();windG.gain.value=0.04;\n  const w=noiseSrc();w.connect(windF);windF.connect(windG);windG.connect(master);w.start();\n  const pad=AC.createGain(),lp=AC.createBiquadFilter();lp.type='lowpass';lp.frequency.value=900;\n  pad.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001,AC.currentTime);pad.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.05,AC.currentTime+4);\n  pad.connect(lp);lp.connect(master);\n  [220,277.18,329.63,415.3].forEach((f,i)=>{const o=AC.createOscillator();o.type=i%2?'triangle':'sine';o.frequency.value=f;o.detune.value=(i-1.5)*4;o.connect(pad);o.start();});\n}\nfunction setWind(speed){\n  if(!AC)return;\n  const k=Math.min(1,Math.max(0,(speed-12)/30)),t=AC.currentTime;\n  windF.frequency.setTargetAtTime(300+k*1600,t,0.15);windG.gain.setTargetAtTime(0.03+k*0.2,t,0.15);\n}\nfunction sfx(name){\n  if(!AC)return;const t=AC.currentTime;\n  if(name==='whoosh'){const s=noiseSrc(),f=AC.createBiquadFilter();f.type='bandpass';f.Q.value=1.5;\n    f.frequency.setValueAtTime(300,t);f.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(2500,t+0.35);f.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(500,t+0.9);\n    s.connect(f);f.connect(env(0.35,0.25,0.65));s.start(t);s.stop(t+1);}\n  else if(name==='chime'){[1318.5,1975.5,2637].forEach((fr,i)=>{const o=AC.createOscillator();o.type='sine';o.frequency.value=fr;\n    o.connect(env(0.18/(i+1),0.005,1.2));o.start(t);o.stop(t+1.3);});}\n  else if(name==='thud'){const o=AC.createOscillator();o.type='sine';o.frequency.setValueAtTime(140,t);o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(35,t+0.45);\n    o.connect(env(0.8,0.005,0.5));o.start(t);o.stop(t+0.6);\n    const s=noiseSrc(),f=AC.createBiquadFilter();f.type='lowpass';f.frequency.value=400;s.connect(f);f.connect(env(0.4,0.005,0.25));s.start(t);s.stop(t+0.3);}\n}\n```\n\n## What each part does\n| Cue | Synthesis |\n|---|---|\n| Wind loop | A 2 s looping white-noise buffer goes through a bandpass filter. In `setWind(speed)`, the speed range 12–42 m/s from the flight spec sets the filter centre (300–1900 Hz) and the gain (0.03–0.23), both smoothed with `setTargetAtTime`. |\n| `sfx('whoosh')` | A bandpass noise sweep from 300 to 2500 to 500 Hz over about 0.9 s. Call it on entering an updraft column. |\n| `sfx('chime')` | Three sine partials (E6, B6, E7) with a 5 ms attack and a 1.2 s decay. Call it on picking up an orb. |\n| `sfx('thud')` | A sine drop from 140 to 35 Hz plus a short burst of low-passed noise. Call it on an island hit or cloud contact. |\n| Ambient chord bed | An A-major-7 chord (A3, C♯4, E4, G♯4) using slightly detuned sine and triangle oscillators through a 900 Hz lowpass. It fades in over 4 s and starts inside `startWind()`. |\n\n## How the game should call it\n- **First user action:** call `startWind()` in the first Space keydown, mousedown or touchstart handler. Later calls only resume a suspended context.\n- **Each fixed step:** call `setWind(v)`.\n- **Events:** call `sfx('whoosh')` when entering an updraft, `sfx('chime')` on an orb pickup, and `sfx('thud')` on game over.\n- **Before the first action:** all three functions return early while `AC` is `null`, so it is safe to call them before that action.\n- **Restart:** no audio reset is needed. Wind and the chord bed keep running, and `setWind` follows the new speed.\n\n## Not yet verified\n- I have not run this code in a browser in this workflow, so audio output, loudness balance and timbre are untested.\n- I have not tested it with autoplay policies in Chrome, Firefox or Safari. iOS Safari may additionally require the call to come from a `touchend` or `click` handler.\n- I have not checked CPU cost on mobile devices. Each `sfx` call creates a few short-lived nodes, and frequent orb pickups have not been profiled.\n- I have not judged the mix against the game's visuals or playtested it alongside the flight model."
