      "output": "## Review record: Cloud-Sea Glide (static source review, not actually run)\n\n**Method:** I read the HTML source only. Nothing was executed in a browser or simulated. Every finding below is a static reading.\n\n**Confirmed in source (matches spec)**\n- **Pitch:** locked for 3 s via `ft<3`. Hold climbs at +0.8 rad/s to 0.35; release dives at −0.25 rad/s to −0.35.\n- **Speed and sink:** speed formula, limits `12+4d`–42, vertical speed and ceiling 140 all match.\n- **Steering:** bank ±0.6 at 2.5 rad/s, returning to 0; turn rate `.9*sin(bank)`.\n- **Updrafts:** `vy+=14` when `h<10&&P.y<150`.\n- **Orbs:** pickup within 4 m; score is `floor(dist/10)+10*orbN`.\n- **Collisions:** island cylinder from top−40 to top+3 with r+1.5; cloud contact at `P.y<=.5`.\n- **Safe start:** first island at `nI=450`; lateral offset ≥40 while `nI<600`.\n- **Best result:** held in `let best=null` only, with no storage API.\n- **Restart:** needs `ot>.6`, accepts Space, click or R, and `reset()` clears objects and flight state.\n- **External requests:** only the three.js r128 CDN script; audio is synthesised.\n\n**Defects found**\n1. **Blocking (static finding):** `THREE.CapsuleGeometry` was added in three.js r139 and does not exist in r128. It is used in `createSky` (`bg=new T.CapsuleGeometry(.12,.5,2,4)`) and in `createGlider` (torso, legs, arms). This should throw \"not a constructor\" before the game loop starts, so the page would likely be blank.\n2. **Stall snap:** stall can push θ to −0.6 (`th=Math.max(-.6,th-.5*dt)`). The next release step, `Math.max(-.35,th-.25*dt)`, then jumps it back to −0.35. Also, once 4d>1 the speed floor exceeds 13, so stall can no longer trigger.\n3. **Camera on restart:** `act()` does not reset `LK`, so after a restart the camera look-at sweeps in from the crash point.\n4. **Collision vs. visuals:**\n   - Arches, windmills and trees rise above top+3 but cannot be hit.\n   - The tapered island underside (`r*.06` at the bottom) collides at full radius.\n   - Cloud puff sprites sit at y = 2–10, above the y = 0.5 contact line.\n5. **Touch steering:** steering with a side-of-screen touch also sets `hold=true`, so a touch player cannot steer while diving.\n\n**Unverified**\n- That the game renders or runs at all (see defect 1).\n- The real no-input time to cloud contact (spec hand estimate is about 11 s) and the feel of updraft lift.\n- Frame rate with 2048 shadows and per-frame updates of the sea vertices.\n- Mobile and touch behaviour.\n- Whether the 3D functions are used exactly as delivered upstream: the original art output was not among the inputs. The integration adds a 0.5 glider scale and enables shadows on the light found by traversing the scene."
